# One target becoming illegal while staying on the battlefield stops the whole exchange too (CR 608.2b, 701.12a: if the
# entire exchange can't be completed, no part of it occurs). Bot1 casts Switcheroo on its Ornithopter and Bot2's Llanowar
# Elves; in response Bot2's Mother of Runes gives the Elves protection from blue, so the blue Switcheroo can no longer target
# it (CR 702.16b). Switcheroo resolves with only the Ornithopter a legal target: both creatures stay where they were.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Sapphire
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Mox Pearl
Island
Ornithopter
Switcheroo
Island x13

[Bot2 Deck]
Plains
Mox Emerald
Mother of Runes
Llanowar Elves
Plains x16

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot2.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Mother of Runes.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Llanowar Elves.Cast
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Switcheroo.Cast
Bot1.Target(Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter; Bot2.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Battlefield.Mother of Runes.Activate(Llanowar Elves)
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Colors(Blue)
? Bot2.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves.ProtectionFrom = Blue
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield = Mox Sapphire; Mox Jet; Mox Ruby; Mox Pearl; Island; Ornithopter
Bot1.Graveyard = Switcheroo
Bot2.Battlefield = Plains; Mox Emerald; Mother of Runes; Llanowar Elves
